Track 2: Kalu’s Chrysalis at Toll Plaza 3
- Story & Context: Written during a fourteen-hour siege inside an abandoned glass toll collector booth, Kalu watched rainfall pooling inside the empty coin hopper while cold copper filings stained his fingertips from endless tambourine repairs. Struggling with the guilt of dragging young marchers into the sights of state water cannons, he whispered an exhausted confession into an omnidirectional boundary mic pressed to the bulletproof glass. The rhythm stuttered with a fragile, hollow hesitation, punctuated by his deadpan vocal mantra: "Patience is a beetle trapped inside a meter."
